# =============================================================================
# reice — a reject guard must name its payload
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • `reice cond iace err` always carries the `iace` particle (en `throw`) and
#     the error value to throw. The particle is mandatory, so a guard that drops
#     it is refused by name (PARSE001 reice_iace).
#   • `reice` is the boolean twin of `requirit`: it desugars to
#     `si (cond) { iace err }`, failing when the condition holds. There is no
#     recoverable failure without something to throw.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • writing the guard as a bare condition — add `iace <error>` after it.
# =============================================================================

main {
    reject 1 ≡ 2
}
